.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_review-changes-02.md:28:3. stop returns as a no-op; the configuration reference remains retained and the generation remains startable.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_review-changes-02.md:31:This violates AC1 because the serialized stop event does not prevent later mutation/revival of the same generation, and AC5 because stop completes with a retained configuration reference instead of the recorded baseline. It also leaves the provider integration vulnerable to a stop/start scheduling inversion around the cross-actor runtime call.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_review-changes-02.md:35:- Make a stop that wins in the initial disconnected state terminally consume or cancel that generation, release its retained configuration reference, and prevent any later start from reviving it.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_review-changes-02.md:36:- Add deterministic coverage for stop-before-start and a stop-wins concurrent start/stop ordering. Assert start cannot proceed, no settings or usable capability is published, repeated stop remains idempotent, cleanup completes once, and resourceFootprint plus the external ledger equal baseline.
