.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-30zng6/TASK-260715-30zng6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log:2074:description:Implement the production dependency factories consumed by ReluxTunnelCore using only the accepted M0 binding manifest from TASK-260720-1qhxqa. For each provider, construct candidate-neutral SSH bootstrap and transport, TCP and DNS consumers, an M1PacketPlaneSession wrapper over the accepted PacketBridge API, PacketFlow, NetworkSettingsPlanBuilder and NetworkSettingsApplier, clocks, metrics, logging, cancellation, memory pressure, and snapshot dependencies. M1PacketPlaneSession.prepare is pure preflight that validates bound configuration and constructs references without acquiring descriptors, HEV resources, the private SOCKS boundary, or PacketFlow reads. Its post-settings activateReads invokes the existing PacketBridge.start and owns the resulting HEV/private-ingress/bridge lifetime. Preserve deterministic harness substitution and prevent provider, HEV C, or selected-engine types from entering coordinator contracts.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-30zng6/TASK-260715-30zng6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log:2075:scope:In scope: binding-manifest schema and digest validation; productionCompositionPermitted enforcement; factory and session protocols; one object graph per runtime generation; pure packet-plane preflight; post-settings activation through the accepted PacketBridge.start API; private-ingress dispatch to TCP CONNECT and virtual-DNS UDP/TCP with other UDP rejected in M1; health and idempotent stop; ownership transfer and reverse release; native library startup and shutdown hooks; accepted dependency pins and configuration values; iOS, macOS and harness compositions; compile-time boundary guards; fail-fast behavior before routes for absent, superseded or incompatible bindings. Out of scope: changing PacketFlowBridge startup semantics, generating or reinterpreting M0 decisions, choosing or tuning engines, MTU, buffers or windows, coordinator transitions, TCP/DNS internals, route policy values, UI, general UDP, lanes and reconnect.
