.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-30zng6/TASK-260715-30zng6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log:3597:ac:1. Start/stop/failure tests prove endpoint A remains bridge-owned, endpoint B is only borrowed, no task is detached, and normal stop, cancellation, startup failure, and runtime failure join all children and the HEV borrow before closing B then A exactly once. 2. Forward sends exactly one [network-order AF word][unchanged IP packet] datagram per valid typed packet; reverse maps exactly one valid datagram to one ordered typed packet, while empty/undersized/unknown/mismatched frames follow the contract counters and zero-length datagrams are not treated as EOF. 3. Both endpoints preserve existing flags while gaining CLOEXEC/NONBLOCK, request both socket buffers, expose all requested/effective byte gauges, and enforce checked count/time work slices and the 4+MTU datagram ceiling without an application queue. 4. Darwin EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK normalize to the canonical would-block counters, ENOBUFS drops without retry, and EMSGSIZE, peer EOF, PacketFlow rejection, and unclassified persistent errors perform the single fatal transition with exact counters and one privacy-safe log. 5. Static inspection and injected-seam tests prove exact metric names/units/monotonicity/maxima, first-error-wins termination, no utun control access, no FD scanning/reopening/duplication, no unbounded retry or side buffer, and no sensitive log fields.
