.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9591:- IMPLEMENTATION: Child initial window/cap/adjustment policy is set through a normal pre-open channel option and observed through snapshots/events; returned credit is earned only after pipeline delivery. Client manual, per-direction protected-byte, and injected-monotonic-time rekeys share the existing KEX state machine, coalesce concurrent reasons/promises, reset generation counters on success, and observe server-initiated KEX without product reflection or a test-only API.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9597:- VERIFICATION: The contract defines every operation, state, timeout/cancellation scope, error, metric, privacy rule, and E-ALGO/E-HOSTAUTH/E-CHANNELS/E-BACKPRESSURE/E-WINDOW/E-REKEY/E-KEEPALIVE/E-CANCEL/E-SCALE/E-ERRORS/E-METRICS-PRIVACY/E-INJECTION row. Three task-scoped PlantUML sources pass syntax checking and their lifecycle, pre-auth host verification, and channel/window/rekey SVG renders were visually inspected.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9607:- DECISION: ADR-014 remains open. Both candidates retain identical host-key, window, sustained 5 GiB rekey, scale (through 1,000 channels), cancellation, algorithm, extension-build, memory, and physical-size gates. Unknowns are named experiments in `.research/260720_task-260715-28ok1k-ssh-engine-candidate-audit.md`; no missing capability was waived.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9615:- REWORK: `requestStop()` now skips upstream quit after the joined main call has returned while preserving listener shutdown and stop metrics. Tests cover both main-return-first and stop-first orderings and fail if quit lands after return.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9616:- REWORK: The loopback listener fd is closed exactly once by its dispatch-source cancel handler on `listenerQueue`; `stop()` waits for cancellation before returning, eliminating the accept-loop fd-reuse window.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9620:- DECISION: The real `DescriptorBorrowConsumer` runs pinned HEV `ad760049` on exactly one dedicated pthread, calls the public quit API once, joins before return, and never closes or duplicates bridge endpoint B. A process-wide lease protects HEV's global C state.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9658:- NOTE for TASK-260715-3dn813: rows not yet exercised at bridge level — pre-send synthetic 4+MTU ceiling fatal, reverse truncation→fatal, readiness `peerClosed` and unexpected-HEV-return, cancellation at every startup barrier stage, drop-summary window suppression, saturation logging. `PacketFlowBridge.runEnded` also carries a cosmetic dead `reachedRunning` branch (both arms set `.failed`).
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9661:- DECISION: `PacketFlowBridge` stores one supervisor plus forward, reverse, and HEV-return child tasks; a first-event control owns fatal/stop selection and cleanup always shuts down reads, cancels readiness, joins both pumps, requests and joins the HEV borrow, then closes B before A exactly once.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9664:- VERIFICATION: Swift Testing covers byte-exact SDK-derived IPv4/IPv6 framing, zero/undersized/unknown/mismatched reverse frames, bounded count/time slices, queue-pressure loss, EMSGSIZE, PacketFlow rejection, first-error-wins, startup cancellation/failure, privacy-safe logging, and 100 restart cycles.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9669:- NOTE for TASK-260715-3o0co4: `PacketFlowAdapterBoundary.writePackets` has no post-shutdown gate (bridge pump must stop writing by construction), and after a cancelled committed read new reads return `readAlreadyPending` until the late NE callback retires the tombstone — expected during shutdown, not an error.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9672:- DECISION: iOS and macOS adapters share one locked `PacketFlowAdapterBoundary`; callback, task cancellation, and terminal adapter shutdown race for one continuation, while the callback registration remains a payload-free tombstone until NetworkExtension invokes it because `NEPacketTunnelFlow` exposes no deregistration API.
