.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9712:+- REGRESSION: A mandatory-health callback could enter after the tracked startup child returned but before the outer `start()` continuation resumed. Because `startupTask` was still retained, the callback deferred cleanup; the outer continuation then cleared the handle and returned success without revalidating actor state, leaving the generation parked in stopping with retained resources.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9713:+- FIX: After joining the startup child, `start()` now rechecks caller cancellation, environment cancellation, lifecycle ownership, and termination while actor-isolated before atomically clearing `startupTask` and returning. A callback that wins the handoff therefore forces the error/cleanup path; a callback that arrives after the atomic handoff observes no startup owner and starts cleanup itself.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9714:+- COVERAGE: A package-internal async handoff hook, following the existing core test-hook pattern, deterministically injects current-generation DNS health loss after child completion and independently pauses the same boundary for caller cancellation. Neither test issues a masking `stop()`; both assert no capability revival, exactly-once reverse cleanup, a zero external resource ledger, and the coordinator baseline footprint.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9717:+### 0120 — M1 coordinator makes settings uncertainty and cleanup ordering explicit (TASK-260715-3tlgwm)
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9718:+- IMPLEMENTATION: `TunnelRuntimeCoordinator` owns one actor-serialized generation and a tracked startup task. It retains each successful acquisition before the next cancellation check, rejects repeat starts, discards mismatched-generation health events, and coalesces caller cancellation, provider stop, startup failure, and mandatory health loss through one shielded cleanup task.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9720:+- CLEANUP: Teardown closes admission, stops packet reads/native work, clears settings when required, then stops DNS, TCP, and SSH in reverse acquisition order. The coordinator releases configuration references and all tracked task/resource handles; repeated stop calls join the same cleanup.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-3tlgwm/TASK-260715-3tlgwm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:9721:+- VERIFICATION: Ten injected startup failures, seven stop/cancellation boundaries, caller cancellation, stale callbacks, 32 concurrent stops, clear failure, snapshot ordering, and 100 generations pass in normal and Thread Sanitizer runs. `make validate-core` passes boundary/native checks, 203 tests in 23 suites, and the post-test build; strict repository Swift format lint, `git diff --check`, and board validation pass.
